.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_GET_STREAM_READ_STATE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_get_stream_read_state ,
.Nm SSL_get_stream_write_state ,
.Nm SSL_get_stream_read_error_code ,
.Nm SSL_get_stream_write_error_code ,
.Nm SSL_STREAM_STATE_NONE ,
.Nm SSL_STREAM_STATE_OK ,
.Nm SSL_STREAM_STATE_WRONG_DIR ,
.Nm SSL_STREAM_STATE_FINISHED ,
.Nm SSL_STREAM_STATE_RESET_LOCAL ,
.Nm SSL_STREAM_STATE_RESET_REMOTE ,
.Nm SSL_STREAM_STATE_CONN_CLOSED
.Nd get QUIC stream state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Fd #define SSL_STREAM_STATE_NONE
.Fd #define SSL_STREAM_STATE_OK
.Fd #define SSL_STREAM_STATE_WRONG_DIR
.Fd #define SSL_STREAM_STATE_FINISHED
.Fd #define SSL_STREAM_STATE_RESET_LOCAL
.Fd #define SSL_STREAM_STATE_RESET_REMOTE
.Fd #define SSL_STREAM_STATE_CONN_CLOSED
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_get_stream_read_state
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_get_stream_write_state
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_get_stream_read_error_code
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "uint64_t *app_error_code"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_get_stream_write_error_code
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "uint64_t *app_error_code"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_state
and
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_state
retrieve the overall state of the receiving and sending parts of a QUIC
stream, respectively.
.Pp
They both return one of the following values:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy SSL_STREAM_STATE_NONE
This value is returned if called on a non-QUIC SSL object, or on a QUIC
connection SSL object without a default stream attached.
.It Sy SSL_STREAM_STATE_OK
This value is returned on a stream which has not been concluded and
remains healthy.
.It Sy SSL_STREAM_STATE_WRONG_DIR
This value is returned if
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_state
is called on a locally-initiated (and thus send-only) unidirectional
stream, or, conversely, if
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_state
is called on a remotely-initiated (and thus receive-only) unidirectional
stream.
.It Sy SSL_STREAM_STATE_FINISHED
For
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_state ,
this value is returned when the remote peer has signalled the end of the
receiving part of the stream.
Note that there may still be residual data available to read via
.Xr SSL_read 3
when this state is returned.
.Pp
For
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_state ,
this value is returned when the local application has concluded the
stream using
.Xr SSL_stream_conclude 3 .
Future
.Xr SSL_write 3
calls will not succeed.
.It Sy SSL_STREAM_STATE_RESET_LOCAL
This value is returned when the applicable stream part was reset by the
local application.
.Pp
For
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_state ,
this means that the receiving part of the stream was aborted using a
locally transmitted QUIC
.Sy STOP_SENDING
frame.
It may or may not still be possible to obtain any residual data which
remains to be read by calling
.Xr SSL_read 3 .
.Pp
For
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_state ,
this means that the sending part of the stream was aborted, for example
because the application called
.Xr SSL_stream_reset 3 ,
or because a QUIC stream SSL object with an un-concluded sending part
was freed using
.Xr SSL_free 3 .
Calls to
.Xr SSL_write 3
will fail.
.Pp
When this value is returned, the application error code which was
signalled can be obtained by calling
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_error_code
or
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_error_code
as appropriate.
.It Sy SSL_STREAM_STATE_RESET_REMOTE
This value is returned when the applicable stream part was reset by the
remote peer.
.Pp
For
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_state ,
this means that the peer sent a QUIC
.Sy RESET_STREAM
frame for the receiving part of the stream; the receiving part of the
stream was logically aborted by the peer.
.Pp
For
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_state ,
this means that the peer sent a QUIC
.Sy STOP_SENDING
frame for the sending part of the stream; the peer has indicated that it
does not wish to receive further data on the sending part of the stream.
Calls to
.Xr SSL_write 3
will fail.
.Pp
When this value is returned, the application error code which was
signalled can be obtained by calling
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_error_code
or
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_error_code
as appropriate.
.It Sy SSL_STREAM_STATE_CONN_CLOSED
The QUIC connection to which the stream belongs was closed.
You can obtain information about the circumstances of this closure using
.Xr SSL_get_conn_close_info 3 .
There may still be residual data available to read via
.Xr SSL_read 3
when this state is returned.
Calls to
.Xr SSL_write 3
will fail.
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_state
will return this state if and only if
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_state
will also return this state.
.El
.Pp
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_error_code
and
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_error_code
provide the application error code which was signalled during non-normal
termination of the receiving or sending parts of a stream, respectively.
On success, the application error code is written to
.Em *app_error_code .
.Sh NOTES
If a QUIC connection is closed, the stream state for all streams
transitions to
.Sy SSL_STREAM_STATE_CONN_CLOSED ,
but no application error code can be retrieved using
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_error_code
or
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_error_code ,
as the QUIC connection closure process does not cause an application
error code to be associated with each individual stream still existing
at the time of connection closure.
However, you can obtain the overall error code associated with the
connection closure using
.Xr SSL_get_conn_close_info 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_state
and
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_state
return one of the
.Sy SSL_STREAM_STATE
values.
If called on a non-QUIC SSL object, or a QUIC connection SSL object
without a default stream,
.Sy SSL_STREAM_STATE_NONE
is returned.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_get_stream_read_error_code
and
.Fn SSL_get_stream_write_error_code
return 1 on success and 0 if the stream was terminated normally.
They return -1 on error, for example if the stream is still healthy, was
still healthy at the time of connection closure, if called on a stream
for which the respective stream part does not exist (e.g.
on a unidirectional stream), or if called on a non-QUIC object or a QUIC
connection SSL object without a default stream attached.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr SSL_stream_conclude 3 ,
.Xr SSL_stream_reset 3 ,
.Xr SSL_new_stream 3 ,
.Xr SSL_accept_stream 3 ,
.Xr SSL_get_conn_close_info 3
.Sh HISTORY
These functions were added in OpenSSL 3.2.
